q 1 0.824 0.11 rg 0 812 595 30 re f Q
BT /F2 10 Tf 40 822 Td (BTechi  |  Statistics - Unit 2: Probability) Tj ET
BT /F2 20 Tf 40 770 Td (1. Basic Probability) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 40 735 Td (Sample space and events) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 40 711 Td (The sample space S is the set of all possible outcomes of an experiment.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 40 694 Td (An event A is any subset of S. Example: rolling a die, S = {1,2,3,4,5,6}.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 40 677 Td (Axioms of probability) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 40 653 Td (1. P\(A\) >= 0 for every event A.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 40 636 Td (2. P\(S\) = 1.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 40 619 Td (3. For mutually exclusive events, P\(A or B\) = P\(A\) + P\(B\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 40 602 Td (Useful rules) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 40 578 Td (Complement: P\(not A\) = 1 - P\(A\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 40 561 Td (Addition: P\(A or B\) = P\(A\) + P\(B\) - P\(A and B\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 40 544 Td (Worked example) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 40 520 Td (A card is drawn from a standard deck. P\(heart or king\) = 13/52 + 4/52 - 1/52 = 16/52.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 270 30 Td (Page 1 of 3) Tj ET
endstream
