7 0 obj
<< /Length 1001 >>
stream
q 1 0.824 0.11 rg 0 812 595 30 re f Q
BT /F2 10 Tf 40 822 Td (BTechi  |  Statistics - Unit 2: Probability) Tj ET
BT /F2 20 Tf 40 770 Td (2. Conditional Probability) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 40 735 Td (Definition) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 40 711 Td (P\(A | B\) = P\(A and B\) / P\(B\), provided P\(B\) > 0.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 40 694 Td (We restrict the sample space to B and ask what fraction of it also lies in A.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 40 677 Td (Multiplication rule) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 40 653 Td (P\(A and B\) = P\(A | B\) P\(B\) = P\(B | A\) P\(A\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 40 636 Td (Independence) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 40 612 Td (A and B are independent if P\(A and B\) = P\(A\) P\(B\), i.e. P\(A | B\) = P\(A\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 40 595 Td (Mutually exclusive events with non-zero probability are never independent.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 40 578 Td (Worked example) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 40 554 Td (P\(A\) = 0.5, P\(B\) = 0.4, independent: P\(A and B\) = 0.5 x 0.4 = 0.2.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 270 30 Td (Page 2 of 3) Tj ET
endstream
