stream
q 1 0.824 0.11 rg 0 812 595 30 re f Q
BT /F2 10 Tf 40 822 Td (BTechi  |  Statistics - Unit 2: Probability) Tj ET
BT /F2 20 Tf 40 770 Td (3. Bayes' Theorem) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 40 735 Td (Formula) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 40 711 Td (P\(A | B\) = P\(B | A\) P\(A\) / P\(B\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 40 694 Td (with P\(B\) = P\(B | A\) P\(A\) + P\(B | not A\) P\(not A\)  \(law of total probability\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 40 677 Td (The base-rate trap) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 40 653 Td (Disease prevalence 1%, test sensitivity 99%, false positive rate 5%.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 40 636 Td (P\(disease | positive\) = 0.0099 / \(0.0099 + 0.0495\) = 0.167, only about 17%.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 40 619 Td (Rare conditions produce more false positives than true positives.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 40 602 Td (Tree method) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 40 578 Td (Draw branches for the prior, then for the evidence; multiply along paths,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 40 561 Td (then divide the path you care about by the total of all matching paths.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 270 30 Td (Page 3 of 3) Tj ET
endstream
